{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-brings-realisations","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:brings-realisations","kind":"remark","title":"Realisations of Bring's surface","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-brings-surface","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-c-quantum-universe"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-brings-surface","cites":["references/kattan2024"],"text":"brings-realisations.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:brings-realisations\"></a><p>Over an archimedean field <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> (e.g. <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Q}</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{R}</code>, or <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{C}</code>), Bring's surface is a compact Riemann surface of genus <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">4</code>. One explicit uniformization: it is the compactification of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{H}/H_4(5)</code>, where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_4(5)</code> is the level-5 congruence subgroup of the Hecke group <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_4</code>, normal of index <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">120</code>; the induced regular map of type <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{5,4\\}</code> has <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">30</code> vertices, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">60</code> edges and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">24</code> faces, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2 - 2g = 30 - 60 + 24 = -6</code> <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"kattan2024\">[kattan2024, §3]</span>. The unit circle bundle <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M_S</code> in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T^*\\Sigma_4</code> is a CR manifold of hypersurface type (real dimension <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3</code>). It provides the archimedean realisation of the quantum observable universe (<a href=\"#ex:c-quantum-universe\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{C}</code>-quantum universe</a>).</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/brings-realisations.md","heading":"Remark","number":"8.4.4","page":"b/rem-brings-realisations","qa":{"counts":{"pass":60,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":60},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
